        "comments": "The assembly drCitBerg1.hap1.1 is based on 70x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Ancient Environmental Genomics Initiative for Sustainability (AEGIS,\nhttps://globe.ku.dk/research/ancient-environmental-genomics-initiative-for-sustainability). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. The order and orientation of the scaffolds on the following regions are unsure: SUPER_1 19.06 Mbp - 25.86 Mbp, SUPER_5 33.48 Mbp - 33.80 Mbp and SUPER_5 35.21 Mbp - 36.28 Mbp",
